## Audit report

Objective: agent-authored 4.5h load wait (`pause for load and resume after 20`) must be bounded with frequent reevaluation, not one blind sleep.

Verified fix in `extensions/loops/goal-tools.ts`: `kind=wait` with `resumeAt` >1h is clamped to `Date.now()+1h`, with user notice and `pause_wait_clamped` ledger. Tool return includes the notice, stored state carries the clamped horizon, short waits pass through. Heartbeat `overdueWaitDue`/`overdueWaitBackstop` re-dispatches overdue waits (90s grace, per-goal:resumeAt key), so a 4.5h request becomes ~4 hourly re-evaluations.

Focused tests pass (13/13): `load-wait-bound` pins both clamp and passthrough; `pause-informativeness` pins the constant and ledger.

No recursion violation: new test uses `MockPi`/`runTool`, does not spawn `bun test`.

